(>> 6.1 Crystal Geometry, Lattices, and Unit Cells) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Solid state physics studies the microscopic atomic architecture and macroscopic physical) Tj
T*
(properties of condensed matter. In civil materials science, crystal structure governs) Tj
T*
(the strength of steel rebar, hydration of Portland cement, and stability of soil clay) Tj
T*
(minerals.) Tj
T*
(* Crystal Lattice: An infinite periodic mathematical array of geometric points in 3D) Tj
T*
(space, where every lattice point has surroundings identical to every other point.) Tj
T*
(* Basis \(Motif\): An atom, ion, or group of atoms attached identically to every) Tj
T*
(lattice point: Crystal Structure = Lattice + Basis.) Tj
T*
(* Unit Cell: The fundamental repeating volumetric building block of a crystal that) Tj
T*
(reproduces the entire crystal lattice upon repeated spatial translations by primitive) Tj
T*
(vectors a, b, c.) Tj
T*
(* Primitive Cell: A minimum-volume unit cell containing strictly ONE lattice point.) Tj
T*
(* Bravais Lattices: In 3D space, exactly 14 unique Bravais lattices exist,) Tj
T*
(categorized into Seven Crystal Systems: \(1\) Cubic, \(2\) Tetragonal, \(3\) Orthorhombic,) Tj
T*
(\(4\) Rhombohedral \(Trigonal\), \(5\) Hexagonal, \(6\) Monoclinic, \(7\) Triclinic.) Tj
T*
