T*
(* Material Classification based on Band Structure:) Tj
T*
(- 1. Conductors \(Metals\): Valence band and conduction band overlap, or conduction band) Tj
T*
(is partially filled. Zero bandgap \(E_g = 0\). Electrons easily accelerate into empty) Tj
T*
(states under tiny applied electric fields.) Tj
T*
(- 2. Semiconductors: Completely filled valence band separated from empty conduction band) Tj
T*
(by a small forbidden energy bandgap \(E_g ~ 0.5 to 2.5 eV, e.g. Silicon E_g = 1.1 eV\).) Tj
T*
(Thermal excitation at room temperature kicks electrons across bandgap, creating) Tj
T*
(conduction electrons and mobile holes.) Tj
T*
(- 3. Insulators: Large forbidden bandgap \(E_g > 5.0 eV, e.g. Diamond E_g = 5.4 eV\).) Tj
T*
(Thermal energy is insufficient to bridge gap; electrical conductivity is negligible.) Tj
T*
