([EXAMPLE 1: Bragg's Law X-Ray Diffraction on Copper FCC Crystal]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: Copper crystallizes in an FCC lattice. An X-ray diffractometer using) Tj
T*
(Cu-K_alpha radiation of wavelength lambda = 0.1542 nm \(1.542 Angstroms\) records the) Tj
T*
(first-order \(n = 1\) reflection peak from the \(1 1 1\) planes at glancing Bragg angle) Tj
T*
(theta = 21.65 deg. Calculate: \(1\) Interplanar spacing d_111, \(2\) Lattice parameter a of) Tj
T*
(copper, \(3\) Atomic radius r of copper, \(4\) Density of copper \(Atomic weight = 63.55) Tj
T*
(g/mol, N_A = 6.022 * 10^23 mol^-1\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Compute Interplanar Spacing d_111 using Bragg's Law:) Tj
T*
(2 * d * sin\(theta\) = n * lambda => d_111 = \(1 * 0.1542 nm\) / \(2 * sin\(21.65\)\).) Tj
T*
(sin\(21.65 deg\) = 0.3689.) Tj
T*
(d_111 = 0.1542 / \(2 * 0.3689\) = 0.1542 / 0.7378 = 0.2090 nm \(2.090 Angstroms\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Compute Lattice Parameter a:) Tj
T*
(d_hkl = a / sqrt\(h^2 + k^2 + l^2\) => a = d_111 * sqrt\(1^2 + 1^2 + 1^2\) = d_111 *) Tj
T*
(sqrt\(3\).) Tj
T*
(a = 0.2090 nm * 1.73205 = 0.3620 nm = 3.620 * 10^-10 m \(3.620 Angstroms\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Compute Atomic Radius r for FCC \(4*r = a*sqrt\(2\)\):) Tj
T*
(r = a * sqrt\(2\) / 4 = 0.3620 nm * 1.4142 / 4 = 0.1280 nm = 1.280 Angstroms.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Compute Theoretical Mass Density rho:) Tj
T*
(FCC unit cell contains n_atoms = 4 atoms.) Tj
T*
(Unit cell volume V_cell = a^3 = \(3.620 * 10^-8 cm\)^3 = 4.7438 * 10^-23 cm^3.) Tj
T*
(Mass of unit cell = \(n_atoms * Atomic Weight\) / N_A = \(4 * 63.55 g\) / \(6.022 * 10^23\) =) Tj
T*
(4.221 * 10^-22 g.) Tj
T*
(rho = Mass / Volume = 4.221 * 10^-22 g / \(4.7438 * 10^-23 cm^3\) = 8.898 g/cm^3 = 8898) Tj
T*
(kg/m^3 \(matches empirical value of 8900 kg/m^3\).) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: d_111 = 0.209 nm; lattice parameter a = 0.362 nm; atomic radius r = 0.128) Tj
T*
