/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: A crystallographic plane in a simple orthorhombic lattice has) Tj
T*
(intercepts at 2a along x-axis, 3b along y-axis, and is parallel to the z-axis \(intercept) Tj
T*
(= infinity\). A second plane intersects axes at 3a, -2b, and 1c. Determine the Miller) Tj
T*
(indices for both planes.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Plane 1 Analysis:) Tj
T*
(Intercepts: \(2a, 3b, infinity*c\).) Tj
T*
(Divide by unit cell dimensions: \(2, 3, infinity\).) Tj
T*
(Take reciprocals: \(1/2, 1/3, 1/infinity\) = \(1/2, 1/3, 0\).) Tj
T*
(Multiply by LCM \(6\): \(3, 2, 0\).) Tj
T*
(Miller Indices for Plane 1: \(3 2 0\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Plane 2 Analysis:) Tj
T*
(Intercepts: \(3a, -2b, 1c\).) Tj
T*
(Divide by unit cell dimensions: \(3, -2, 1\).) Tj
T*
(Take reciprocals: \(1/3, -1/2, 1/1\).) Tj
T*
(Multiply by LCM \(6\): \(2, -3, 6\).) Tj
T*
(Represent negative index with bar: \(2 bar-3 6\).) Tj
T*
(Miller Indices for Plane 2: \(2 3_bar 6\).) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Plane 1 = \(3 2 0\); Plane 2 = \(2 -3 6\) or \(2 3_bar 6\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
