([EXAMPLE 3: Fermi Energy, Velocity and Temperature in Copper]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: Copper is monovalent with one free conduction electron per atom. Free) Tj
T*
(electron density is n = 8.49 * 10^28 m^-3. Calculate: \(1\) Fermi Energy E_F at 0 K in) Tj
T*
(Joules and electron-volts, \(2\) Fermi Velocity v_F of electrons at Fermi surface, \(3\)) Tj
T*
(Fermi Temperature T_F.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Compute Fermi Energy E_F:) Tj
T*
(E_F = \(h_bar^2 / 2*m_e\) * \(3 * pi^2 * n\)^\(2/3\).) Tj
T*
(h_bar = 1.05457 * 10^-34 J-s; m_e = 9.109 * 10^-31 kg.) Tj
T*
(Constant term: h_bar^2 / \(2 * m_e\) = \(1.05457 * 10^-34\)^2 / \(2 * 9.109 * 10^-31\) = 6.104) Tj
T*
(* 10^-39 J-m^2.) Tj
T*
(3 * pi^2 * n = 3 * \(3.14159\)^2 * 8.49 * 10^28 = 29.6088 * 8.49 * 10^28 = 2.5138 * 10^30) Tj
T*
(m^-3.) Tj
T*
(\(2.5138 * 10^30\)^\(2/3\) = [ \(2.5138\)^\(2/3\) ] * 10^20 = 1.8488 * 10^20 m^-2.) Tj
T*
(E_F = \(6.104 * 10^-39\) * \(1.8488 * 10^20\) = 1.1285 * 10^-18 Joules.) Tj
T*
(In eV: E_F = 1.1285 * 10^-18 J / \(1.6022 * 10^-19 J/eV\) = 7.043 eV.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Compute Fermi Velocity v_F:) Tj
T*
(0.5 * m_e * v_F^2 = E_F => v_F = sqrt\( 2 * E_F / m_e \).) Tj
T*
(v_F = sqrt\( 2 * 1.1285 * 10^-18 / 9.109 * 10^-31 \) = sqrt\( 2.4777 * 10^12 \) = 1.574 *) Tj
T*
