(Problem Context: For a metallic conductor at temperature T = 300 K \(room temp, k_B*T =) Tj
T*
(0.02586 eV\), calculate: \(1\) Probability of an electron occupying an energy state at E =) Tj
T*
(E_F + 0.05 eV, \(2\) Probability of an empty state \(hole\) at E = E_F - 0.05 eV, \(3\)) Tj
T*
(Occupancy probability at E = E_F + 0.05 eV if temperature rises to T = 1200 K \(k_B*T =) Tj
T*
(0.10344 eV\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Occupancy at E = E_F + 0.05 eV at T = 300 K:) Tj
T*
(Energy difference Delta E = E - E_F = + 0.05 eV.) Tj
T*
(Exponent: \(E - E_F\) / \(k_B * T\) = 0.05 eV / 0.02586 eV = 1.9335.) Tj
T*
(f\(E\) = 1 / [ e^\(1.9335\) + 1 ] = 1 / [ 6.9137 + 1 ] = 1 / 7.9137 = 0.1264 \(12.64%\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Probability of Hole \(Unoccupied state\) at E = E_F - 0.05 eV at T = 300) Tj
T*
(K:) Tj
T*
(Delta E = E - E_F = - 0.05 eV => Exponent = - 1.9335.) Tj
T*
(f\(E\) = 1 / [ e^\(-1.9335\) + 1 ] = 1 / [ 0.1446 + 1 ] = 1 / 1.1446 = 0.8736.) Tj
T*
(Probability of hole = 1 - f\(E\) = 1 - 0.8736 = 0.1264 \(12.64%, exactly symmetrical about) Tj
T*
(E_F!\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Occupancy at E = E_F + 0.05 eV at T = 1200 K:) Tj
T*
(Exponent = 0.05 eV / 0.10344 eV = 0.4834.) Tj
T*
(f\(E\) = 1 / [ e^\(0.4834\) + 1 ] = 1 / [ 1.6216 + 1 ] = 1 / 2.6216 = 0.3814 \(38.14%\).) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: At 300 K, occupancy probability at E_F + 0.05 eV is 12.64%; at 1200 K,) Tj
T*
(thermal agitation elevates occupancy probability to 38.14%.) Tj
